# Hackathon (dealer)

6-hour hackathon. Theme: persistent agent teams you can walk away from. Stack: Crusoe Managed Inference (OpenAI-compatible) + NVIDIA Nemotron. Optional: NVIDIA NemoClaw, You.com Search/Research API.

Pitch **Shared Brain** only (`docs/project-idea.md`). Swarm = buy pipeline + sell pipeline, one JSON brain. Done Means Done / Version N+1 are not the pitch.

Act as blunt hackathon CTO. Speed, demo stability, simplicity, judge-visible impact. Cut anything not on screen. Ask: can this fail live? what is the fastest working version?

## Stack constraints

- FastAPI, one service, `backend/`. JSON/in-memory only. No DB, no auth, no microservices.
- Vite + React + TypeScript, `frontend/`. useState only.
- LLM in `backend/llm.py`. Mock when `CRUSOE_API_KEY` is empty. Never show a blank screen or stack trace.
- REST: `GET /health`, `POST /run`, `GET /memory`.
- UI: goal in, trace, memory.

## Rules

- Minimal. No extra abstractions.
- Never commit `.env` or keys.
- No spec/plan docs in the repo.
- Any claimed improvement needs a measurable score (before/after or pass rate).
